// THE TRAVERSALS — what writings have undergone. One object or one crossing per line.
//
// Built 2026-08-17 on Kevin's mark, "build the traversal organ."
//
// WHAT IS IN HERE: object references and crossings. An object is {store, i, sha}
// — an index into an append-only store and a digest. THERE IS NO TEXT IN THIS
// FILE and there is no field that could hold any. The display law's own test for
// its fourth source is "strip every model's output text out of the record; if a
// display state changes, that state was reading content." Nothing to strip.
//
// WHAT IT IS SEEDED WITH, AND WHY ONLY THIS: the one traversal this session can
// attest to — the vision draft going out to three readings tonight. Kevin's
// actual practice has months of circulation in it and none of it is on disk. I
// am not reconstructing it from his description, because a traversal store
// seeded from an account of traversals is exactly the fault the standing spine
// was built to catch: a record with a provenance and no support.
//
// SO THE STORE IS SMALL AND TRUE RATHER THAN LARGE AND REMEMBERED. His own
// history enters when a hand enters it, one crossing at a time, or not at all.
//
// TWO OF THE THREE BRANCHES BELOW ARE STILL OUT. They carry no `to`, which is
// in-flight — not ended, not held. Nothing was inferred from their silence and
// nothing here asks after them.
//
// Run:  node tools/traversal_check.js

// EVERY OBJECT DECLARES ITS SEAT, and the seat is one of the twelve. It is
// DECLARED BY THE HAND, never inferred — the same rule the surface label obeys,
// for the same reason: an organ that works out where a writing belongs is a
// classifier, and it would be the fifth source wearing the fourth's coat.
//
// All seven below are seated at LENS, and that is a READING rather than a
// derivation. The seat's gesture is "I WORK IT UNTIL IT HOLDS", and every object
// here is a draft being worked. Strike it and it costs only these rows.
//
